  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In Threshold Tate Shaw has composed a kind of travel literature for the global age where a place can be many places at once or no place at all. Tate’s writing gives us patient, winding directions telling us what to do and think along the way. The spaces in his simple photographs seem to be notes made that we are inclined to forget in our everyday movements. Between the photos, text, and through turning the pages of this pocket-sized book, is a circuitous narrative about thoughts and sensation." Publisher's website.</subfield>
